course: dictionary
lesson: 527
title: A word for a person in space
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Context is the words around a word. They often tell you what it means. Read this: «Astronauts' muscles and bones weaken in space, so they exercise about two hours every day.» The words in space and weaken tell you that astronauts are people who go into space, and they must work hard to stay strong there.
explain: Look for clues in other sentences too. «The first people on the Moon were the American astronauts Neil Armstrong and Buzz Aldrin.» Here the Moon is a place, and astronauts are the people who went there. Ask yourself: what kind of person could travel to the Moon? That answers it.
explain: Some words have a special name in another country. «Russian astronauts are called cosmonauts.» Cosmonaut and astronaut mean the same kind of person, but the word depends on the country. If you meet a new word like this, check the context first, then a dictionary.
fact: An astronaut is a person trained to travel and work in space.
fact: Astronauts wear spacesuits outside because there is no air to breathe in space.
fact: On the International Space Station, astronauts float because they are in free fall around the Earth.
fact: Neil Armstrong and Buzz Aldrin were American astronauts and the first people to walk on the Moon.
fact: Russian astronauts are called cosmonauts.
exercise: What is an astronaut? | *A person trained to travel and work in space | A scientist who studies stars through a telescope on Earth | A large rocket that carries fuel
exercise: «Astronauts' muscles and bones weaken in space, so they exercise about two hours every day.» What do astronauts do every day to stay strong? | Eat only sweets | Sleep for twelve hours | *Exercise for about two hours | Swim in a pool
exercise: What is the name for a Russian astronaut? | Pilot | Rocket | Spacewalk | *Cosmonaut
test: Why do astronauts wear spacesuits when they go outside the space station? | *Because there is no air to breathe in space | Because the spacesuits keep them warm on a sunny day | Because the station is too heavy to carry | Because spacesuits make them float
test: «The first people on the Moon were the American astronauts Neil Armstrong and Buzz Aldrin.» Who were the first people on the Moon? | Dogs in a rocket | Russian cosmonauts | *Neil Armstrong and Buzz Aldrin | Yang Liwei
exam: Which phrase means the training that prepares a person to go into space? | *astronaut training | space station | spacewalk | naked eye
